// expect: refuse E_FieldOffsetUnprovable
// EXPECTATION TRUED TWICE. 2026-07-25 (the resolved-or-loud offset
// landing): the old banked value was the PARTIAL-SET offset read — the
// arm's demanded {beta | rho} summed offsets over {beta} alone, so .beta
// read offset 0, the receiver's first SORTED field (alpha); the full set
// resolves through the row residual or floors LOUDLY. This arm's rho is
// genuinely free — the op param is polymorphic across performs, so no
// install's key closes it — and the floor trapped at run time (134).
// 2026-09-28 (R0″): the floor is said at the settle point and the compile
// refuses with zero bytes, where it had trapped.
// Rung 3c: same as rung 3b but ops renamed so the WRITER (aset) sorts BEFORE
// the reader (zrd). If alphabetical arm-typing order is the cause — the read
// snapshotting the state type before the write lands — this passes while
// rung 3b (rd<set, reader-first) traps. That would pin the root: the state
// READ re-derives a snapshot instead of carrying the live handle (#7).
effect P {
  aset(x)
  zrd() -> a
}

handler h with s = {alpha: 0, beta: 0, gamma: 0} {
  aset(v) => resume() with s = v,
  zrd() => resume(s),
}

fn run() with P + Memory + Alloc = {
  aset({alpha: 1, beta: 2, gamma: 3})
  zrd()
}

fn main(q) = (run() ~> h).beta
